  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47501\", \"PowerToys#36451\", \"PowerToys#45730\"], \"answer\": \"This crash has been reported before. The stack trace matches PowerToys#47501 and #45730 exactly. It is a WPF 'Cyclic reference found while evaluating the Style property' error on a ListView with 15 items. It is thrown from ThemeManager.OnSystemThemeChanged when Windows broadcasts a theme change. Maintainers believe the source is the PowerToys Run result list, even though the ticket was filed under 'General'. The Windows 11 update or the VM boot probably triggered a theme or accent refresh as PowerToys was starting. Older tickets with a ScrollViewer variant of the same error were closed as duplicates of #36451, and the same theme-change trigger appears there. I found no fix or workaround in the archived tickets. Please add your bug report and details to #36451 or #47501. Say whether the crash coincided with a theme or accent change, an automatic light/dark switch, or a resume from sleep. In the meantime, the crash dialog is most likely harmless. You can restart PowerToys manually after boot, or delay its start-up until the desktop has finished loading.\"}",
